d. A mismatch could prolong stale authority reporting or request admission, but no incorrect commitment, stale application read, or public completion has been established.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"src-contact\",\n          \"src-heartbeat\",\n          \"src-append-reply\",\n          \"src-snapshot-reply\",\n          \"src-pipeline-reply\",\n          \"src-stale-stepdown\",\n          \"src-initialize\",\n          \"src-lease\",\n          \"src-lease-contract\",\n          \"src-lease-purpose\",\n          \"src-reject-old\",\n          \"src-verify\",\n          \"src-register-verify\",\n          \"src-verify-vote\",\n          \"src-leader-cleanup\",\n          \"src-stepdown-consume\",\n          \"src-lease-timer\",\n          \"src-verify-contract\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"Local leader main thread\",\n          \"Independent heartbeat and replication workers\",\n          \"Remote configured voter\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"followerReplication.lastContact\",\n          \"AppendEntriesResponse.Term and Success\",\n          \"local leader role\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"Fixed voter membership proposed for first discriminator\",\n          \"One leader-state allocation and term\",\n          \"Remote receiver with higher current term; legal prefix unresolved\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"Initialize contact marker -> heartbeat RPC -> higher-term negative reply -> local contact refresh -> lease consumer\",\n          \"Ordinary replication higher-term reply -> stepDown channel -> Follower\",\n          \"Pending VerifyLeader -> false heartbeat vote -> main-thread Follower\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-initialize\",\n          \"b-heartbeat\",\n          \"b-append-contact\",\n          \"b-snapshot-contact\",\n          \"b-pipeline-contact\",\n          \"b-lease-consume\",\n          \"b-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"fact-peer-contact-marker\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"b-old-request-reject\": \"Actual receiver branch can produce a newer-term rejection; same-execution higher-term acquisition is still unknown.\",\n          \"b-negative-verify\": \"Independent negative-verification path can invalidate authority despite refreshed lease contact.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"LeaderLeaseTimeout explicitly promises step-down without quorum contact, not on every rejected reply.\",\n          \"Source describes lease as heartbeat-connectivity checking rather than a read-only query lease.\",\n          \"Ordinary, snapshot and pipeline reply paths check higher terms before refreshing contact.\",\n          \"Pending VerifyLeader can step down on a negative heartbeat response.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Applicable requirement gap: no acquired source yet requires the heartbeat path itself to act on a higher reply term. Asymmetry is not a normative obligation.\",\n          \"Initial-prefix gap: establish a real elected leader and a remote higher term with fixed membership, rather than assigning internal state.\",\n          \"Same-history gap: ordinary reply delays must be finite; protective workers, incoming RPCs and verification must be accounted for.\",\n          \"Endpoint gap: source traces bookkeeping only; role retention and externally effective consequences have not been executed or observed.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 2,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Independent heartbeat refreshes shared evidence without the term comparison found in three adjacent producer paths; its consumer retains a local authority role using marker age. Next read the transport and replication progress contracts and relevant authority-loss expectations, then choose a controlled same-history exploration only if the requirement gap remains actionable.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stage\": \"analyze\",\n      \"read_plan_id\": null,\n      \"material_ids\": [],\n      \"spec_task_ids\": [],\n      \"stagnation\": 0,\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Register the initial partial map and preserve a concrete A2 contact-marker question. Code establishes heterogeneous marker qualification; documentation weakens a naive successful-acknowledgement interpretation. No obligation or Evidence is claimed. Next discriminator is applicability of higher-term response handling and whether independent replication or incoming RPC processing necessarily closes the suspected window.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [],\n  \"claims\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"assessments\": [],\n  \"frontier\": {\n    \"surfaces\": [\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"Raft.startStopReplication membership update/removal branches\",\n        \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [],\n        \"reason\": \"Only allocation branch acquired; fixed-membership scope proposed.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"src-initialize\"\n        ],\n        \"high_consequence\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"Raft.processRPC and election paths\",\n        \"disposition\": \"UNCLASSIFIED_PROTOCOL_RESPONSIBILITY\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [],\n        \"reason\": \"Dispatch is observed but handlers and election prefix are not yet mapped; could provide independent authority invalidation.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"src-stepdown-consume\"\n        ],\n        \"high_consequence\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"Pipeline transport completion/error contract\",\n        \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [],\n      